    "score": 50,
    "text": "Hi HN!<p>Utpal here, I&#x27;m one of the founders of OpenComputer.<p>OpenComputer is an open source cloud coding agent for teams that can run in your own cloud account (AWS, GCP, Azure).<p>We run the agent harness and the sandbox on the same durable VM (architecture in the docs [1]). First commit lands in 24s; the alternatives we benchmarked took 53-72s (benchmarks below [2]).<p>Two other choices:<p>- One VM per team, scalable horizontally. Sessions are isolated in git worktrees.\n- Session files are backed up to a repo after every turn, so any session can resume on another VM.<p>We noticed that past ~640 session-hours a month, one always-on 4 vCPU VM is cheaper than per-session E2B sandboxes, for example. So at scale, this setup would not only be faster than current SOTA coding agents, but also more cost-efficient.<p>Feel free to try via cloud for free [4] or self host. We would love any and all feedback, and happy to answer any questions! Full demo below [3].<p>[1]: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;docs.opencomputer.dev&#x2F;getting-started&#x2F;architecture\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;docs.opencomputer.dev&#x2F;getting-started&#x2F;architecture</a>\n[2]: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;opencomputer.dev&#x2F;blog&#x2F;cloud-agents-as-fast-as-local&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;opencomputer.dev&#x2F;blog&#x2F;cloud-agents-as-fast-as-local&#x2F;</a>\n[3]: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;x.com&#x2F;IgorZIJ&#x2F;status&#x2F;2121309785882591711\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;x.com&#x2F;IgorZIJ&#x2F;status&#x2F;2121309785882591711</a>\n[4]: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;app.opencomputer.dev\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;app.opencomputer.dev</a>",
    "time": 1795205996,
    "title": "Show HN: OpenComputer – an open source alternative to Devin",
    "type": "story",
    "url": "https://github.com/diggerhq/opencomputer"
  },
